# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# Stella agent workspace. The root `.stella/` is per-workspace scratch
# (sessions, exports, private evidence) and stays ignored — with one tracked
# exception: `commands/`. A custom slash command only steers a teammate's
# session if it travels with the repository, so commands are reviewed through
# the same pull requests as the code. Mirrors the exception macanderson/stella
# makes for `.stella/rules/`.
!/.stella/
/.stella/*
# Commands are opt-in, one command per line, rather than a blanket negation:
# `.stella/commands/` is also where locally-generated scratch commands land,
# and a command only belongs in review if someone meant it to travel. Four
# lines are required, in this order -- git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so dropping the first makes the rest inert.
!/.stella/commands/
/.stella/commands/*
!/.stella/commands/triage-sweep.md
!/.stella/commands/triage-sweep.toml
